(text "Lira: nRF52840 (Ebyte E73-2G4M08S1C), USB-C + Li-Po, 57 keys, built-in USB sound card" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 18 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "de1815e5-baf2-4db0-95b6-e44f824e287b"))
(text "Power / USB / programming copied from the BlueMicro840 (jpconstantineau/NRF52-Board), a board built with this module, assembled by JLCPCB and sold. Differences from it:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d9d30f2c-791e-4f06-bdb7-ea0d81a44083"))
(text "1. Second AP2112K (switched 3.3 V for external devices, P0.12 enable) omitted: nothing external to power." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f4ca2841-14ca-4b13-b6f1-9eace5807df2"))
(text "2. USBLC6-2SC6 ESD array added on D+ / D- / VBUS at the USB-C receptacle." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 30.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e005698c-8409-42f1-a7f3-4ca2e0f36d38"))
(text "3. Power switch SW101 (C&K JS102011SAQN, 300 mA) in the battery + line, as on ZMK keyboards; JP2 bypasses it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 33.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "97fa9f40-687c-48d3-99cd-1a788a7e0e62"))
(text "4. JP1 + R104: closing the solder jumper puts a second 10k on PROG: charge current 100 mA -> 200 mA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 36.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a3fac968-0fd8-4fa3-99cb-793fd4b33c69"))
(text "5. Reset push button SW102 to GND (the BlueMicro840 has only a test point)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 39.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2f560b7e-4b01-4a77-8b6c-9359ec854264"))
(text "6. USB-C shield pads to GND (left open on the BlueMicro840)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 43 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "689d5348-dc2a-4a0e-96e6-534a4ccd11fe"))
(text "7. LEDs: charging LED white, status LED red on P1.04 only (BlueMicro840: green charging, red P1.04, blue P1.10)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 46.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cc7bfb45-d566-430c-9744-18b91a298c4d"))
(text "8. DCCH inductor pads (DNP on the BlueMicro840) not fitted at all; P1.10 is a free GPIO here, P1.02 switches the sound card." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 49.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b1bf5a28-3723-4454-9ced-a95df0399941"))
(text "9. Test points added on VBUS, VBAT and VIN (BlueMicro840: SWDIO, SWCLK, VCC, GND, RESET, P1.02)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 52.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a2cc4134-ae70-44b1-ae77-642b06dd774d"))
(text "10. C107 4.7 uF added on VBUS at the charger's VDD pin (the MCP73831 datasheet asks for 4.7 uF; Nordic's reference circuit has 4.7 uF on VBUS; the BlueMicro840 has none)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 55.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "72d75720-0e08-4cbe-88be-fa0d1c37dec9"))
(text "11. C108 1 uF at the regulator output and C109 100 nF at the module: the 10 uF C103 sits at the module's supply pins (VDD / VDDH), 25 mm away. C102 on VIN is 1 uF instead of 10 uF: together they keep the capacitance charged at USB attach near USB 2.0's 10 uF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "25fc5845-d4d5-4921-93aa-be7491231882"))
(text "12. Charger MCP73831 instead of the TP4054, same pins and same PROG resistor (1000 V / R_PROG): it is stable with no battery, so the board also works when built without one (its STAT pin, and the white LED, stay off)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 62.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "00e3cb74-4d0d-4a4d-b497-ac4442ba32eb"))
(text "13. Battery divider 10M + 10M with 10 nF (BlueMicro840: 806k + 2M, 1 nF): the MCP73831 recognises a missing battery only if VBAT sees more than 7 MOhm (datasheet 4.2); 10 nF >= 2^12 x the SAADC's 2.5 pF keeps the reading within 1 LSB (Nordic, 'Measuring Lithium battery voltage with nRF52'), and RMK samples it every 30 s. Drain 0.2 uA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 65.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0ae1a38d-f5cc-4816-a0ed-1c303eeb1166"))
(text "14. Built-in USB sound card: the USB-C data lines go (through the ESD array) to a CH334P hub; hub port 3 goes to the module's D+ / D-, port 2 to a CM108B codec (C-Media demo board v1.33) with a 3.5 mm headset jack." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 68.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3505db39-78f7-4f08-bbf4-19f01198bba9"))
(text "USB-C (sink: 5.1k on each CC) and ESD protection" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 62 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "33e09af5-5427-498b-af63-0823d578cc09"))
(symbol (lib_id "Connector:USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0_16P") (at 44.45 95.25 0) (unit 1) (exclude_from_sim no) (in_bom yes) (on_board yes) (dnp no) (uuid "019dc34d-1708-4f42-935f-43f4c28bb32b")
